Beginner’s Guide to Motor Insurance in Kenya

What is Motor Insurance?
Motor insurance protects vehicle owners against financial loss caused by accidents, theft, fire, or legal liability.

---

Types of Motor Insurance

1. Third Party Insurance
Covers:
- Injury to third parties
- Damage to third-party property

Does NOT cover:
- Damage to your own vehicle

Best for:
- Budget-conscious vehicle owners
- Older vehicles

---

2. Comprehensive Insurance
Covers:
- Accidents
- Theft
- Fire
- Malicious damage
- Third-party liability

Best for:
- Newer vehicles
- Higher-value cars

---

How to Choose Cover
Consider:
- Vehicle value
- Usage (private or commercial)
- Budget
- Risks in your area
- Claims reputation of insurer

What To Do After an Accident
✅ Stay safe  
✅ Document the scene  
✅ Take photos  
✅ Notify your insurer immediately  
✅ Report to police if required  
✅ Begin claims process


Common Mistakes to Avoid
❌ Underinsuring your vehicle  
❌ Choosing based on price only  
❌ Not reading policy exclusions  
❌ Delaying claims notification

